    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>I'm Giang Truong Vu, also known as Zang Vu or @zvwgvx. My main interests are cognitive AI, backend engineering, cybersecurity and distributed systems.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="section-block">
    <h2>What I work on</h2>
    <p>On the research side, I'm interested in how memory, beliefs, affective state and social context can contribute to persistent AI agents. AELIA, under SENTIA Lab, is the main environment where I explore these questions.</p>
    <p>On the engineering side, I work on backend infrastructure, security-related agent tooling and distributed networking. RiFT focuses on agentic security systems and isolation; Lattice focuses on networking, trustworthy node identity and distributed resources.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section-block">
    <h2>Technical background</h2>
    <p>My work spans algorithms, backend services, tool orchestration and lower-level systems. I use Python, Rust, TypeScript, JavaScript and Node.js according to the constraints of a particular project rather than treating one language as a specialization.</p>
